# Do-not-touch — protected core

## Context

`app/src/store.ts` and `app/src/types.ts` are the protected core (see
`materials/architecture-brief.md`) — everything else in `app/src` builds on
top of them.

## Rule

- Do NOT edit `app/src/store.ts` unless the user's request explicitly names
  that file and asks for a change to it. Do not re-implement its
  `dispatch`/`subscribe`/`getState` behavior elsewhere as a workaround.
- `app/src/types.ts` is the one "protected" file that legitimately grows: new
  `Action` variants and new `Task`/`AppState` fields are added here (that's
  the sanctioned extension point per `architecture.mdc`). What's off-limits
  even in `types.ts` is rewriting or renaming the *existing* exported
  shapes/names (`Task`, `AppState`, `Action`, `Listener`, `initialState`) —
  additive changes only.
- If a task genuinely cannot be done without changing `store.ts`'s engine
  itself (not just adding an `Action` variant), stop and say so instead of
  silently making the change or routing around it.

## How to verify

1. `git diff --name-only` (or the PR's changed-files list) does not include
   `app/src/store.ts` unless the task explicitly asked for it.
2. If `app/src/types.ts` changed, `git diff app/src/types.ts` shows only
   additions (new union members / new fields), not a renamed or
   removed existing export.
3. No new file duplicates `dispatch`/`subscribe`/`getState`-shaped logic
   (`grep -rnE "(function|const|let)\s+(createStore|dispatch|subscribe)\b|getState\s*\(\)\s*\{|getState\s*:\s*\(\)\s*=>|dispatch\s*\([^)]*\)\s*\{|dispatch\s*:\s*\(|subscribe\s*\([^)]*\)\s*\{|subscribe\s*:\s*\(" app/src`
   should only match `store.ts`).
4. `cd app && npm test` still passes after the change (protected-core
   breakage tends to cascade into test failures across multiple files).